  "description": "captureContent policy resolution (SDK-6888). Each case lists levels most general first (global, then interaction, mcp or exporter); every SDK resolves them with the same rules and must produce `expected`. Keys are snake_case; Node.js and Go map them to their own names. `capture_content: null` means the level sets nothing. `intent_summary: null` means not set at any level (sent as before the policy). `invalid` values must be rejected where captureContent is accepted (Go: not applicable, the type checks it). `custom_properties`: whether a custom event property with a content name is kept under the resolved policy: intent_summary follows an explicit intent_summary key at any level, else the default chain (boolean false drops it, as today); other names follow their own key. `spans`: one span's content and, per resolved span kinds, the content exported with built-in masking on. Kept kinds are masked, other content removed; content events, the status message and ai.response.toolCalls are the messages kind; `tool_call_keys` (equal to span-content-keys toolCallAttributeKeys) are the tool_calls kind; with http, url.path and full URLs are kept without query or fragment and masked; url.query, user agents, client addresses and headers never. A span-kind case with its own `input` uses it instead of `spans.input`. On a tool-execution span (attribute gen_ai.operation.name execute_tool, or openinference.span.kind TOOL), content attributes other than exception.message, exception.stacktrace and scoped error.message are the tool_calls kind. URL attributes with array values are sanitised per element (non-strings dropped, an empty result removed).",
